00246:   "claim_to_check": {
00247:     "current": "WP19 describes a common remaining-space minimum mode for battle/items/debug and admits normal template255 storage. WP42 defers exact EV math to it. These read clauses do not describe the reversed interval failure when a255 value reaches the EV allocator.",
00248:     "favorable_existing_scope": "WP28 line350 explicitly limits its252/510 increment guarantee to starting from constrained state. This is contrary evidence against treating item255 as an unconditional contradiction; preserve that qualifier and decide whether the new failure only needs a bounded failure note or no required revision.",
00249:     "not_claimed": "No claim that default factory/tower battles allocate EVs; pbOrganizedBattleEx sets internalBattle=false, so ordinary pbGainExp returns before allocation."
00250:   },
00251:   "producer_chain": [
00252:     {
00253:       "source": "CRE001-S02",
00254:       "fact": "Default line5 CATERPIE template names two distinct effort fieldsHP/ATK."
00255:     },
00256:     {
00257:       "source": "CRE001-S01",
00258:       "fact": "Template creation at L50/IV31 returns a normal non-Shadow creature with currentHP-EV255, ATK-EV255 and otherEV0; final recalculation does not normalize those stored fields."
00259:     }
00260:   ],
00261:   "counterexample": {
00262:     "kind": "SOURCE_STATIC finite direct consumer input; NOT_EXECUTED",
00263:     "premises": [
00264:       "FixedR loaded definitions and fixed six-main-stat order, HP first.",
00265:       "All identity/creation dependencies are valid and normal; no plugin or expression override.",
00266:       "Create the exact default CATERPIE two-effort-field template at L50/IV31 with a valid trainer; creation normally returns P.",
00267:       "For direct battle allocation put the same P atpbParty(0)[0], normal non-Shadow, valid six-key EV vector. Current and restoration item EV modifiers either have no handlers or return normally without changing stored EVs; no virus effect is needed.",
00268:       "Defeated object has valid creature EV-yield data; default CATERPIE givesHP yield1, all other yield0. A separate zero-yield fixture shows zero gain does not guard the interval check.",
00269:       "Invoke the EV allocation helper directly, or conditionally reach it through pbGainExp with internalBattle=true, expGain=true, valid current player participant and defeated/captured foe. These are explicit finite input conditions, not asserted default facility reachability."
00270:     ],
00271:     "input_values": {
00272:       "current_EV": {
00273:         "HP": 255,
00274:         "ATTACK": 255,
00275:         "DEFENSE": 0,
00276:         "SPECIAL_ATTACK": 0,
00277:         "SPECIAL_DEFENSE": 0,
00278:         "SPEED": 0
00279:       },
00280:       "EV_total": 510,
00281:       "HP_yield": 1,
00282:       "default_single_cap": 252,
00283:       "default_total_cap": 510
00284:     },
00285:     "first_difference": "At the firstHP field the remaining single-field allowance is−3. The allocator requests a lower bound0 and upper bound−3; Ruby integer clamp rejects the reversed interval before HP-EV mutation. It does not safely return zero, reduce255 to252, or apply the natural-language minimum as−3.",
00286:     "ordinary_control": [
00287:       "With all currentEV0, HP yield1 allocates1 normally.",
00288:       "WithHP/ATK252/252 (total504), HP yield1 clips to0, all other zero yields complete without the negative single-field interval.",
00289:       "Normal organized facility battle has internalBattle=false; calling ordinary pbGainExp exits before this allocator regardless of template255.",
00290:       "With a single-field255 receiver but current total below510, the same first single-field interval still fails; total capacity does not repair it."
00291:     ],
00292:     "normal_cancel_exception_partial": [
00293:       "The direct allocator has no confirmation/cancel branch.",
00294:       "For the firstHP255 fixture, no receiver EV, experience or growth statistic is changed by this allocator before the failure; producer state255 already exists. Modifier side effects are excluded by the explicit premise.",
00295:       "If reached through ordinary growth, EV allocation precedes this receiver experience grant and participant-list clearing; those later actions are not reached. Earlier processed receivers/callbacks are not promised rollback.",
00296:       "If a later fixed stat is first over-cap, earlier valid stat writes can remain; this broader prefix case is a related static facet, not the minimal firstHP fixture.",
00297:       "A malformed total>510, Shadow savedEV sum that makes allowance negative, and purification addEV use related patterns. They require individual premises and are not automatically added as mandatory scope from the two-field template case."
00298:     ]
00299:   },
00300:   "item_related_facet": {
00301:     "status": "PENDING_B_RECEPTION_NOT_CANONICAL_REQUIRED_SCOPE_YET",
00302:     "facts": "TheHPUP effect directly calls the EV-raising helper with generation-configured100 cap; HEALTHFEATHER passes cap-disabled. With currentHP-EV255, default cap-disabled helper reaches the same reversed0..−3 interval before returning a success Boolean. In100-cap mode the explicit>=100 guard returns0 before this failure. Quantity helper floors its presented minimum at1 even when remaining space is negative.",
00303:     "scope_preservation": "WP28 line350 constrained-state qualification is already correct. Full bag/party wrapper eligibility, inventory persistence and cancellation need B reader before any end-to-end resource claim."
00304:   },
00305:   "negative_evidence": {
00306:     "completed_text_read": [
00307:       "WP19 entire1–268",
00308:       "WP20 entire1–256 (existingPP negative-clamp failure contrasts same language primitive)",
00309:       "WP42 §4.1–4.2 actual read59–85; /root/combat_review independently full-read entireWP42",
00310:       "WP57 entire1–116",
00311:       "WP28 only1–95 and227–232/350 relevant fragments; whole document remains unread by proposer"
00312:     ],
00313:     "literal_locator_searches": "Located252/255/EV/反转 inWP19/WP42/WP28 and sourceallocation/template. This helps locate evidence, not a claim to full semantic absence over all131formal.",
00314:     "gap_boundary": "FullWP28/test-catalogs, all default facility entry combinations and all extra EV helpers have not been semantically accepted. Root must not promote the candidate beyond this read scope."
00315:   },
00316:   "impact": "A future implementation that turns the supplied remaining-space phrase into safe clipping can diverge from the reference for a bounded valid-producer composition. The practical default facility path is protected by its internalBattle gate; broad default runtime impact is unproven.",
00317:   "minimum_correct_revision_proposed": [
00318:     "Clarify the remaining-allowance rule only for inputs with nonnegative remaining per-field and total room; preserve normal252/510 increment and255 template creation/storage contracts.",
00319:     "If this source failure is in mandatory coverage, document that separately reaching the allocator with a stored field already over252 produces a reversed-interval error before that field increment; do not idealize it as safe no-effect/normalization.",
00320:     "Add the valid-template255 direct-allocator vector and normal facility-gate countercontrol. Decide item and Shadow/purification facets only after their actual owning readers check premises and wrappers.",
00321:     "Retain all existing GR-016 creation examples and default facility no-growth behavior; no reference-source changes or new framework implementation."
00322:   ],
